  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="28">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 28</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>K. ⁊ word ⁊ weorc freonda gehwilc fadige mid rihte ⁊ að ⁊ wedd wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>And word ⁊ weorc fréonda gehwilc fadige mid rihte ⁊ að ⁊ wed wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="28" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="98" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ word ⁊ weorc freonda gehwilc fadige mid rihte ⁊ að ⁊ wedd wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="170" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And word and weorc freonda gehwilc fadige mid rihte, and að and wedd wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="255" ed="#liebermann"/>Und ordne der <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_28.lnote.de.1"/>Freunde jeglicher Wort und Werk gerecht und halte sorgsam Eid und Versprechen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let each of [our] friends order his words and deeds rightly and keep oath and pledge carefully.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_28.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="99" ed="#robertson"/>And everyone of our friends<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VIAtr_28.robnote.n.2"/> shall order his words and deeds aright, and strictly abide by his oath and pledge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="171" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And all of our friends must order their words and deeds properly, and carefully uphold their oath and pledge.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:VAtr_22-2">V Atr 22.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 22, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_44-1">VIII Atr 44.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:Cn1020_14">Cn 1020 14</ref>; <ref target="clause:ICn_19-1">I Cn 19.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="342"><label>expanded</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_23">V Atr 23–25</ref> <quote>V 23 – 25, VI 28 – 30 (again expanded)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><ref target="clause:ICn_19-1">I Cn 19.1–2</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_28.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 6. Benutzt durch I Cn 19, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 6. Used by I Cn 19, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_28.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 22, 2; I Cn. 19, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_28.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 6.</seg></note>
      </div>
